  "body_html": "<h1>Mixed Strategy Simplex</h1>\n<p>For a finite set $S$, the mixed strategy simplex $\\Delta(S)$ is the set of\nprobability vectors on $S$:\n$$\n  \\Delta(S)=\\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^S : x_s \\ge 0 \\text{ for all } s,\\ \n  \\sum_{s \\in S} x_s = 1\\}.\n$$\nThe Lean library uses Mathlib's <code>stdSimplex ℝ S</code> for this set, with\n<code>stdSimplex.pure i</code> for the Dirac point mass at $i$ and <code>wsum x f</code> (a\ndefinitional abbreviation for the dot product <code>x ⬝ᵥ f</code>) for the weighted\nsum of a function $f \\colon S \\to \\mathbb{R}$.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Chapter 2, Section 2.3] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. Delta(S) is the simplex of probabilities on a finite set S.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
